{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here because you weren't feeling well—can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I’ve just been really tired. Started a few days ago. I had a runny nose and cough, thought it was from the AC at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any nausea, vomiting, or stomach pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I had some cramps and threw up a couple times. One loose stool, but nothing bloody."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your insulin—have you been taking it regularly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… I missed a couple doses. I was just so tired, I forgot. I usually take Lantus at night and Humalog as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We also saw your blood sugar was very high—over 700—and your body’s in a state called diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA. That’s why you feel so unwell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no… like last time? That was scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, similar. But we’re going to treat it right away. You’re getting fluids through your IV to rehydrate, and we’ve started an insulin drip to bring your sugar down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why my potassium was high too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. High blood sugar pulls fluid and electrolytes out of your cells, which affects potassium. But with fluids and insulin, it’s already starting to come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My mouth’s been so dry, and I’ve been peeing a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s from the high sugar—your kidneys are trying to get rid of it. We’ll fix that. We also checked your kidney function, and it’s a bit impaired from dehydration, but it should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2160-06-23 12:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve been drinking beer—maybe three six-packs a week. Last one was two days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. That can definitely affect your diabetes control and contribute to DKA. But your alcohol level was zero now, and no signs of withdrawal, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to drink anymore. It’s just hard sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can help with that. We’ve started you on thiamine and folate—important vitamins that can be low with alcohol use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to know. What about my cough and runny nose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray—it looks clear, no pneumonia. Your symptoms are likely from a mild cold or allergies. We can give you loratadine if you’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. My eyes are sensitive to light too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2160-06-23 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with DKA. It should get better as your sugars normalize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2160-06-23 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. Your labs are improving—your acid levels are coming back to normal, and your potassium is now in a safe range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2160-06-23 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Is the insulin drip going to stay on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2160-06-23 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll transition you to your regular insulin tonight—Lantus at bedtime with Humalog as needed. The goal is to get off the drip by 9 PM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2160-06-23 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. I just don’t want to end up here again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2160-06-23 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work on that. Staying on your insulin, even when you’re not feeling well, is key. And cutting back on alcohol will help a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re off the insulin drip and doing well on your regular shots. Blood sugars are between 100 and 180."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! I feel a little better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One thing—we checked your iron levels and found they’re low. You have iron deficiency anemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know that. Any bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. We don’t know the cause yet, but we’re starting you on ferrous sulfate—a daily iron pill—to help build it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it. Should I get tested more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2160-06-23 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your doctor will want to look into it further after discharge—maybe check your stomach or intestines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2160-06-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2160-06-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Less tired. I had a low sugar this morning though—felt shaky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2160-06-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we caught it—it was asymptomatic, but we gave you glucose paste. It’s common when adjusting insulin. We lowered your Lantus from 36 to 32 units to prevent that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2160-06-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So I’ll take 32 at night now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2160-06-24 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And keep using Humalog with meals based on your sugar. We’ll make sure you have supplies when you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2160-06-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function has improved—creatinine is back to normal. That means the dehydration is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2160-06-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ll drink more water at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2160-06-24 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please do. And keep monitoring your sugars. If you’re sick, don’t stop insulin—even if you’re not eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2160-06-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your blood cultures came back negative—no infection. That’s great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2160-06-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my cold wasn’t making me worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2160-06-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might have contributed, but it’s not serious. The main issue was missing insulin and drinking alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2160-06-25 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’re doing really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2160-06-25 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2160-06-25 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take your insulin as prescribed—32 units Lantus at night, Humalog as needed. Take the iron pill daily. Stop drinking alcohol. And follow up with your primary doctor in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2160-06-25 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to come back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2160-06-25 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. If you need support with alcohol or depression, let us know—we can connect you with resources."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. We’ve given you prescriptions for insulin, iron, and your blood pressure medicine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll take care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—monitor for dizziness, shortness of breath, or if your sugars go too low or high. Call your doctor or come back if that happens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll check my sugars four times a day like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re doing the right things. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2160-06-26 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Dr. Lee."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2160-06-23 12:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2160-06-26 15:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of alcohol use, was admitted with malaise, fatigue, and DKA due to insulin noncompliance and recent alcohol use. She presented with profound hyperglycemia, metabolic acidosis, and acute kidney injury from dehydration. She was treated in the ICU with IV fluids and an insulin drip, then transitioned to subcutaneous glargine and lispro. Her electrolytes and renal function normalized, and she had one episode of mild hypoglycemia. Iron studies revealed iron deficiency anemia, and she was started on ferrous sulfate. No infection was found. She was discharged home on day 4 with adjusted insulin, iron supplementation, and instructions to abstain from alcohol and follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Hypovolemia",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
